Let's analyze the addition problem:
\begin{tabular}{ccccc} & C & A & S & H \\ + & & & M & E \\ \hline O & S & I & D & E \end{tabular}
From the ones column, we have $H+E = E$ or $H+E = 10+E$.

Now the addition becomes
\begin{tabular}{ccccc} & C & A & S & 0 \\ + & & & M & E \\ \hline O & S & I & D & E \end{tabular}
In the tens column, we have $S+M = D$ or $S+M = 10+D$.

Now the addition becomes
\begin{tabular}{ccccc} & C & A & S & 0 \\ + & & & M & E \\ \hline 1 & S & I & D & E \end{tabular}
From $C+1=S$, we have $S=C+1$.
